  "articleSummary": "The article argues that for security agents, the relevant question is not which model is \"best\" overall, but how to route tasks to the right model based on cost, speed, and evidence quality. Drawing on product-shaped evals for ExploitHunter.app, it shows that cheap models can outperform premium ones on specific tasks, and that many failures stem from system integration (runners, parsers, stores) rather than the model itself. The tone is analytical and engineering-focused, reframing model selection as a routing problem rather than a leaderboard decision. The intended audience is developers building production security agents who need practical deployment guidance over abstract rankings.",
